{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "or-t31-mcp-sessions-2026-11-09",
    "name": "OpenRegister MCP server sessions (needs memcache)",
    "description": "@newman exclude needs a Nextcloud distributed cache (memcache.distributed, e.g. APCu or Redis): MCP sessions created by `initialize` are stored there, and on an instance without one every session-gated JSON-RPC call answers -32000 \"Invalid or expired session\". The CI Newman instance configures no memcache.\n\nLane T31: the session-gated half of POST /api/mcp (McpServerController#handle): ping, tools/list as admin and as a non-admin with their own session, unknown method (-32601), tools/call without a name and resources/read without a uri (-32602). The session-free half (initialize, missing/unknown session, parse/shape errors, notifications, anonymous refusal) runs in CI in openregister-api-entityrelations-gdprentities.postman_collection.json.\n\nSELF-SEEDING: `00 setup` creates its own schema, register, object and two non-admin users with a random per-run suffix; `99 teardown` deletes them. Variables: base_url (default http://localhost:8080), admin_user, admin_password. Basic auth at collection level.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "basic",
    "basic": [
      {
        "key": "username",
        "value": "{{admin_user}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "password",
        "value": "{{admin_password}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
